Let me standardize.

In block world:

- (on X Y) means X is on top of Y. So Y is the block below X.

- (clear X) means there is no block on top of X, so X is the top block.

- (on-table X) means X is on the table.

In initial state:

- (on b1 b3) : b1 is on top of b3 → so b3 has b1 on top

- (on b3 b5) : b3 is on top of b5 → b5 has b3 on top

- (on b5 b4) : b5 is on top of b4 → b4 has b5 on top

- (clear b2) : b2 has no block on top (so b2 is top block)

- (on b2 b1) : b2 is on top of b1 → b1 has b2 on top

- (arm-empty) : arm not holding

- (on-table b4) : b4 is on table

